{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#515","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#515","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#515\",\"parent_revision\":\"aadd93eb38b215a97c98a2f46dc6577a9754e3babfb562f93c2b9b5066276405\",\"root_revision\":\"aadd93eb38b215a97c98a2f46dc6577a9754e3babfb562f93c2b9b5066276405\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-04-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/ecosystem_registry.py:get_ecosystem_owned_keys()` unions only `skill_frontmatter_keys` across registered ecosystems, ignoring `agent_frontmatter_keys`. The sibling function `get_ecosystem_for_key()` correctly checks both fields. This inconsistency means agent files using ecosystem-owned keys would not be protected by the guard set built from `get_ecosystem_owned_keys()`. Current impact is zero because `agent_frontmatter_keys` is empty for all registered ecosystems, but the data model supports future ecosystems and the inconsistency is a latent correctness bug. The fix should union both fields and update the docstring. A test covering the `agent_frontmatter_keys` branch in `get_ecosystem_for_key()` is also missing and must be added.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nClaim 1: agent_frontmatter_keys is empty frozenset() for all registered ecosystems.\\nVerdict: VERIFIED \u2014 ecosystem_registry.py line 60: agent_frontmatter_keys=frozenset() in the opencode EcosystemSpec.\\n\\nClaim 2: get_ecosystem_for_key() correctly checks both skill_frontmatter_keys and agent_frontmatter_keys.\\nVerdict: VERIFIED \u2014 ecosystem_registry.py lines 103-104: `if key in spec.skill_frontmatter_keys or key in spec.agent_frontmatter_keys`.\\n\\nClaim 3: No existing test covers the agent_frontmatter_keys branch.\\nVerdict: VERIFIED \u2014 grep found zero occurrences of 'agent_frontmatter_keys' in plugins/plugin-creator/tests/.\\n\\nClaim 4: _ECOSYSTEM_OWNED_SKILL_KEYS unions only skill_frontmatter_keys.\\nVerdict: VERIFIED \u2014 ecosystem_registry.py lines 74-76: `frozenset().union(*(spec.skill_frontmatter_keys for spec in _REGISTRY.values()))` \u2014 agent_frontmatter_keys generator is absent.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nGoal: Fix get_ecosystem_owned_skill_keys() to union both skill_frontmatter_keys and agent_frontmatter_keys, update its docstring, and add a test covering the agent_frontmatter_keys branch in get_ecosystem_for_key().\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED\\nDate: 2026-04-30\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Source file location | AVAILABLE \u2014 plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/ecosystem_registry.py lines 74-76\\n2. Bug description | AVAILABLE \u2014 names exact lines, missing union, sibling function already correct at line 90-104\\n3. Test file location | AVAILABLE \u2014 plugins/plugin-creator/tests/test_ecosystem_registry.py\\n4. Current impact | AVAILABLE \u2014 zero; agent_frontmatter_keys=frozenset() in all registered ecosystems (confirmed line 60)\\n5. Fix scope | AVAILABLE \u2014 union both fields in _ECOSYSTEM_OWNED_SKILL_KEYS, update docstring, add one missing test\\n6. Dependencies | AVAILABLE \u2014 stdlib-only module; pytest already present in project\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-06T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-06T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **fix agent_frontmatter_keys inconsistency in ecosystem_registry** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task \u2014 code review follow-up from plan/tasks-27-multi-ecosystem-plugin-creator-followup-3.md\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-24)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nReproduction command (no code changes required):\\n\\n```bash\\nuv run python3 -c \\\"\\nimport sys; sys.path.insert(0, 'plugins/plugin-creator/scripts')\\nfrom ecosystem_registry import EcosystemSpec, get_ecosystem_owned_skill_keys\\n# Simulate what the guard set WOULD contain if an ecosystem registered agent keys\\n# Current guard set:\\nprint('guard set:', get_ecosystem_owned_skill_keys())\\n# Expected to contain agent keys too, but cannot because lines 74-76 omit them\\nprint('agent_mcp in guard set:', 'agent_mcp' in get_ecosystem_owned_skill_keys())\\n# Output: False \u2014 bug confirmed\\n\\\"\\n```\\n\\nExpected output before fix:\\n```text\\nguard set: frozenset({'mcp'})\\nagent_mcp in guard set: False\\n```\\n\\nRoot design cause: `_ECOSYSTEM_OWNED_SKILL_KEYS` at line 74-76 uses a generator comprehension that references only `spec.skill_frontmatter_keys`. The `EcosystemSpec` dataclass has had `agent_frontmatter_keys` since it was defined, but the module-level pre-built frozenset never included it. The design intent \u2014 a single guard set for ALL ecosystem-owned keys \u2014 was never fully implemented for agent keys.\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n1. `uv run pytest plugins/plugin-creator/tests/test_ecosystem_registry.py` passes with no failures.\\n2. Test file contains a test explicitly targeting the `agent_frontmatter_keys` branch of `get_ecosystem_for_key()`.\\n3. Guard-set function unions both `skill_frontmatter_keys` and `agent_frontmatter_keys`.\\n4. Docstring of guard-set function no longer refers only to skill keys.\\n5. `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/plugin-creator` exits 0 with no new errors.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\nPriority: P1\\nEffort: Small\\nRationale: Two-line fix to the generator comprehension plus one new test case. No API changes required (function name and return type unchanged). No migration or multi-file coordination needed. Zero risk of regression since agent_frontmatter_keys is currently empty for all registered ecosystems.\\nEstimated implementation: < 30 minutes\\n\\n### Scope\\n\\nget_ecosystem_owned_keys() unions only skill_frontmatter_keys, ignoring agent_frontmatter_keys.\\nSibling function get_ecosystem_for_key() already checks both fields correctly.\\nFix: union both fields in the guard-set function, update docstring, add missing test branch.\\nImpact: zero currently (agent_frontmatter_keys is empty in all ecosystems), but latent correctness bug.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `_ECOSYSTEM_OWNED_SKILL_KEYS` is rebuilt from both `skill_frontmatter_keys` and `agent_frontmatter_keys` for every registered ecosystem\\n- [ ] A test ecosystem registered with `agent_frontmatter_keys=frozenset({\\\"agent_key\\\"})` causes `\\\"agent_key\\\"` to appear in the function's return value\\n- [ ] `get_ecosystem_for_key()` existing behaviour is unchanged (already correct)\\n- [ ] A new pytest test explicitly exercises the `agent_frontmatter_keys` branch in `get_ecosystem_for_key()` \u2014 the test must fail before the fix and pass after\\n- [ ] Docstring of `get_ecosystem_owned_skill_keys()` references both `skill_frontmatter_keys` and `agent_frontmatter_keys`\\n- [ ] `uv run pytest plugins/plugin-creator/tests/test_ecosystem_registry.py` exits 0 with no failures\\n- [ ] `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/plugin-creator` exits 0 with no new errors\\n\\n### Prior Work\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Source | plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/ecosystem_registry.py |\\n| Tests | plugins/plugin-creator/tests/test_ecosystem_registry.py |\\n| Validator | plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/plugin_validator.py |\\n| Docs | plugins/plugin-creator/references/ARCHITECTURE.md |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\nDepends on: None\\nBlocks: None \u2014 latent correctness bug, no current consumer is broken\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\nAlignment assessment: ALIGNED\\n\\nThe module docstring states its purpose: 'declares which top-level YAML frontmatter keys belong to external AI tool ecosystems'. The EcosystemSpec dataclass documents two distinct key sets: skill_frontmatter_keys and agent_frontmatter_keys. The sibling function get_ecosystem_for_key() already checks both \u2014 establishing the design intent that both key types are part of the ecosystem ownership model.\\n\\nFix aligns with design intent: unioning both key sets in the guard-set function completes the original design. No new design decisions are introduced. The fix does not expand scope, change the public API, or alter the registered ecosystems.\\n\\nCitation: ecosystem_registry.py lines 1-18 (module docstring), lines 37-55 (EcosystemSpec dataclass), lines 90-104 (get_ecosystem_for_key already correct).\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\nSystems Inventory:\\n\\n| System | File | Impact |\\n|--------|------|--------|\\n| Bug site | plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/ecosystem_registry.py:74-76 | _ECOSYSTEM_OWNED_SKILL_KEYS built from skill_frontmatter_keys only |\\n| Test gap | plugins/plugin-creator/tests/test_ecosystem_registry.py | No test covers agent_frontmatter_keys branch of get_ecosystem_for_key() |\\n| Module docstring | plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/ecosystem_registry.py:25 | Shows get_ecosystem_owned_skill_keys in usage example \u2014 rename/update if function renamed |\\n| Future ecosystems | Any EcosystemSpec with non-empty agent_frontmatter_keys | Their agent keys would be silently excluded from guard set |\\n\\nBlast radius: CONTAINED \u2014 zero production callers affected today (agent_frontmatter_keys is empty for all registered ecosystems). Risk is forward-only: surfaces when a future ecosystem registers agent-specific keys.\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\nType: defect\\nRationale: The function `_ECOSYSTEM_OWNED_SKILL_KEYS` / `get_ecosystem_owned_skill_keys()` was written to build a complete guard set of all ecosystem-owned frontmatter keys, but the implementation never included `agent_frontmatter_keys` from the `EcosystemSpec` dataclass. The data model is correct; the materialization of the guard set is incomplete. This is a latent correctness bug \u2014 the defect exists in the code today even though its impact is currently zero.\\nAnalysis method: Direct code inspection (lines 54, 74-76, 90-104 of ecosystem_registry.py)\\nScenario target: Forward compatibility \u2014 any future ecosystem registering agent_frontmatter_keys will have those keys silently excluded from the guard set\\n\",\"digest\":\"484cbfbba993807289d6e003ed171ec52f212fcb612c000279e4720b6918d68a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCtj7Q\"}"}